# Template drift allowlist for zudo-css-wisdom.
# Generated projects start from create-zudo-doc templates; this file lists
# intentional divergences from the pinned create-zudo-doc baseline so
# `pnpm check:template-drift` exits 0.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line (no leading slash).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# Reconciled against the create-zudo-doc 4.4.13 baseline, the first time this
# check has ever run in this repo (it was added together with the rest of the
# guard set — see Takazudo/zudo-css-wisdom#183). Every entry below was diffed
# individually; each one keeps a host customization that adopting the template
# version would silently destroy. Nothing is listed merely to make the check
# green.
#
# The 4.4.x base template tracks only five files (tsconfig.json,
# pages/index.tsx, pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx, src/styles/global.css,
# scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh) plus one i18n feature file; everything else in
# this repo is host-owned and not template-tracked at all.

# ── docHistory-patched route stubs ────────────────────────────────────────
# create-zudo-doc patches the base + i18n doc-route stubs when the docHistory
# feature is selected: it statically imports DocHistory from
# "@takazudo/zudo-doc/doc-history" and merges it over chromeBindings in
# createChrome's hostBindings, so the doc-history button hydrates on these
# self-contained dynamic routes. `docHistory: true` is set in zfb.config.ts, so
# the patch is correct here. Verified against the 4.4.13 templates: the
# DocHistory import + the defineChromeBindings spread are the ONLY differences —
# both files are otherwise byte-identical to the template, so they are already
# on the 4.4.x baseline and carry no stale drift.
pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx
pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx

# ── Host brand customization: global.css ──────────────────────────────────
# global.css carries host brand overrides on top of the v4 base template: the
# Noto Sans JP `--font-sans` stack (theme.css defaults to system-ui), the
# `--font-futura` brand face, and the `[data-header-logo]` Futura header rule.
# Everything else (design tokens, base rules, feature CSS) ships from
# @takazudo/zudo-doc via theme.css / content.css / features.css.
src/styles/global.css

# ── (retired) Wide home page override ─────────────────────────────────────
# `pages/index.tsx` used to be listed here: it was a hand-reconstructed route
# rendering HomePageView with `wide`, because zudo-doc 4.2.1 exposed no config
# toggle for the wide home grid. The pattern originated in this repo
# (css-wisdom PR #182) and upstream tracked it as zudolab/zudo-doc#2959.
#
# zudo-doc 4.4.x ships `home: { wide?: boolean }`, read by BOTH the
# package-owned root and locale index routes, so the override is gone:
# pages/index.tsx is back to the stock 1-line re-export (and the sibling
# pages/[locale]/index.tsx override was deleted outright). The entry is
# deliberately NOT replaced — the file is now template-identical and the drift
# check actively verifies that.

# ── tsconfig.json: load-bearing, do NOT adopt the template version ────────
# The template ships a 3-line config that `extends
# "@takazudo/zudo-doc/tsconfig.base.json"` and sets
# `include: ["src", "pages", "zfb.config.ts"]`.
#
# This repo instead inlines the base compilerOptions and uses `exclude` with NO
# `include`. That is not stale copy-paste — it is what keeps the repo's own
# root-level `zfb-shim.d.ts` inside the tsc program. With no `include`, tsc
# picks up every file under the project root (minus `exclude`), so the shim's
# ambient `declare module "zfb/config"` is compiled; under the template's
# `include` allowlist the root-level shim is silently dropped. Measured with
# `tsc --listFiles`: host config = zfb-shim.d.ts present, template config =
# absent.
#
# That matters because zfb-shim.d.ts is the hand-synced source of truth for the
# `ZfbConfig` type that `zfb check` binds against (see the long comment at the
# top of that file — an ambient declare-module wins over node resolution and
# over tsconfig `paths`). Adopting the template would type-check zfb.config.ts
# against the package's shim instead, silently changing which contract the
# config is validated against.
#
# Note: the template version does pass `pnpm check` today, so the breakage
# would not be immediate — it would surface later as a config field that the
# hand-maintained shim knows about and the package shim does not, or vice
# versa. That is exactly the silent-drift class this guard set exists to stop.
#
# Two host additions here are vestigial rather than load-bearing and could be
# cleaned up separately: the unused `#doc-history-meta` path alias, and several
# `exclude` entries for directories this repo does not have (e2e/fixtures,
# packages, vendor, src/**/__tests__, scripts/__tests__, vitest.config.ts).
tsconfig.json

# ── scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh: repo-specific skill wiring ────────────────
# The template's generic version derives the skill name from package.json as
# `<projectName>-wisdom` — which would produce `zudo-css-wisdom-wisdom` here.
# This repo pins the skill name to `css-wisdom` (the name referenced by
# scripts/generate-css-wisdom.js, .gitignore, and the published `/css-wisdom`
# global skill) and hard-fails on any override, instead of accepting one via
# `$1` / `$SKILL_NAME` as the template does. The host version is also wired to
# the generate-css-wisdom.js pre-step that builds SKILL.md, which the template
# knows nothing about. Adopting the template would rename the skill and break
# the symlink in ~/.claude/skills/.
scripts/setup-doc-skill.sh

# ── Host brand favicons: do NOT adopt the template set ────────────────────
# zudo-doc 5.0.0 added a default favicon set to the base template
# (favicon.ico + 16x16/32x32 PNGs + favicon.svg) and emits the SVG link
# AHEAD of the .ico/.png entries. The template artwork is a generic purple
# "Z" placeholder; this repo ships its own orange (#ff9900) "C" mark across
# all four files, so adopting the template would replace real branding with a
# placeholder — and because the SVG link comes first, it would win outright.
#
# public/favicon.svg is new here: it carries this repo's own "C" artwork, not
# the template's. It was added precisely so the 5.x SVG-first favicon link
# resolves to the host brand instead of 404ing.
#
# Note for whoever touches these next: public/favicon.ico is not an ICO file —
# it is SVG markup under a .ico name (`file(1)` reports "SVG Scalable Vector
# Graphics image"). That predates this migration and is left as-is here rather
# than fixed silently inside a dependency bump.
public/favicon.ico
public/favicon-16x16.png
public/favicon-32x32.png
public/favicon.svg
